The types Block, BlockTypes, ITextRendering, and KernelArguments are internal or inaccessible, so I cannot directly mock or instantiate them in the test. Also, the RenderCodeAsync method is not virtual and cannot be overridden for testing.

I will write a test that uses a real CodeBlock instance constructed with a real token list, and a real ILoggerFactory with a mock ILogger to verify the LogTrace call. I will create minimal stub classes for the required internal types to simulate the behavior needed for the test.

I will submit a test file that covers the LogTrace call on line 87 by enabling trace logging and verifying the logger received the expected trace message.

